# @hsk-sync:note-meta

Token `@hsk-sync:note-meta` marks shared **note title / note date** resolution.

If priority, parsing rules, or date formats change here, update the sibling implementations and consider how Android list captions, VS Code tree labels, and pyssg HTML `<title>` will look.

## Sibling implementations

| Block | Path |
|-------|------|
| Python (pylib, source of truth) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-pylib\src\harrix_pylib\note_meta.py` |
| VS Code (JS) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-swiss-knife\vscode\harrix-notes-explorer-hsk\note-meta.js` |
| Android (this repo) | `NoteMetaResolver.kt`, `NoteTitleExtractor.kt`, list date captions |

## Shared contract

### Title

1. YAML `title:`
2. Else first `#` heading
3. Else `titleFromId(fileStem)` (part after `__`, `-`/`_` → spaces, title case)
4. Else `Untitled`

### Date

1. Date fragment in file name (`YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYY.MM.DD`, `YYYYMMDD`, `DD.MM.YYYY`)
2. Else YAML `date:`
3. Else file ctime / birthtime when available
4. Else file mtime

Filename/YAML dates display as date-only; file timestamps keep time-of-day in the list.
